Package: leandro-host
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Silas Müller <github@silasmueller.de>
Depends: adduser
Recommends: nvidia-driver-@BRANCH@-open (>= @DRIVER@), nvidia-driver-@BRANCH@-open (<< @DRIVER@.0), nvidia-compute-utils-@BRANCH@ (>= @DRIVER@)
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/UniStuttgart-IKR/Leandro
Description: Leandro host side: GPU paravirtualisation over virtio-nvrm
 vhost-user-nvrm, the backend that serves one guest's virtio-nvrm device from
 the host's NVIDIA driver; upstream vhost-device-input; vgpuprofile, which reads the
 card's vGPU-shaped profiles; and cloud-hypervisor @CH@ with Leandro's
 generic-vhost-user patches, as /usr/lib/leandro/cloud-hypervisor so it does
 not shadow a distribution cloud-hypervisor. All statically linked.
 .
 The host driver must be exactly @DRIVER@ with the open kernel module, in
 persistence mode (nvidia-persistenced). An orchestrator such as the
 MeisterStack agent starts the backends itself; leandro-backend@.service is
 for a cloud-hypervisor driven by hand.
